1
00:00:01,501 --> 00:00:02,961
Uday Raj Aaley: Apart from this,

2
00:00:02,961 --> 00:00:04,129
we, Kusunda language,

3
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:05,588
tell me why did we [you] stop speaking.

4
00:00:05,588 --> 00:00:06,005
Hmm...

5
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:09,884
Gyani Maiya Sen-Kusunda: First went the language.

6
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:10,802
Old men, old women,

7
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:14,389
young men, young women—all

8
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:15,306
Hmm...

9
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:17,308
There is no one who speaks the language,

10
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:18,351
There is no Kusunda (person) either.

11
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:20,854
I...only I speak the (Kusunda) language.

12
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:22,981
There is no one who speaks the language.

13
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:25,233
We don't have a language...

14
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:26,443
We speak bad...bad language.

15
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:29,279
Children...boys and girls don't know the language.

16
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:32,157
Women and men went to villages.

17
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:34,534
People have gone to villages.

18
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:36,661
There is no language.

19
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:38,997
This is not even our language.

20
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:41,541
None speaks the language anymore.

21
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,334
Forgotten the language...Everyone has forgotten the language. 

22
00:00:43,334 --> 00:00:45,295
Our language...language speakers are gone...

23
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:47,088
only two–three people are left.

24
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:48,548
No language left...No language left...

25
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:50,383
there are many people, Kusundas, without the language.

26
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,510
People speak...Kusunda [people]...

27
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:54,596
None..(people) have forgotten the language.

28
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:55,889
Forgotten!

29
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,015
Hmm...Forgotten!

30
00:00:57,015 --> 00:01:00,894
(Laughing) Hmm...(men) have married other (non-Kusunda) girls.

31
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,896
Girls have left with other (non-Kusunda men).

32
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:05,106
Hmm...hmm...

33
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:06,274
Hmm...hmm...everyone has left for villages.

34
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:07,984
Men and women have gone to villages.

35
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:08,735
Hmm...

36
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,695
Girls of villages...

37
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:14,157
(A) wife, husband, forgets the language.

38
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,200
Hmm...

39
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,576
Who will teach?

40
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:18,787
Everyone who spoke the language died.

41
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:20,705
Everyone has forgotten.

42
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:23,082
(goat bleating)

43
00:01:23,082 --> 00:01:25,668
Go and learn the language...come on...come on...others.

44
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:28,087
There are many who don't speak the language.

45
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:29,964
None except me knows the language.

46
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:32,300
No language.

47
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,344
None.

48
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:35,428
None...over...

49
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:36,387
It's over...over...

50
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:37,972
It's done.

51
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:41,518
Done...language finished...language finished ...

52
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:43,019
Hmm...finished!

53
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:47,398
Now to save this Kusunda language

54
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:48,983
Not now...to protect...Hmm...

55
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:51,861
..to make others speak out too, now...Hmm...

56
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:53,655
..what would you say?

57
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:57,867
I will speak the language as long as I live.

58
00:01:57,867 --> 00:02:03,164
None will speak after I die.

59
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,707
There is no language

60
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:05,750
We don't learn, we don't learn new,

61
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:09,754
Not a single person can speak [Kusunda]...cannot speak. 

62
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:10,797
..cannot speak. 

63
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:15,635
(Kusunda is) not learnt...It should be learnt...None speaks.

64
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:18,388
(It) will die...will die that way...nobody will give.

65
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:21,140
Even elders don't speak.

66
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:23,101
You are not Kusunda.

67
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:26,855
Villagers come, they say they won't teach.

68
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:30,525
I won't give (teach) the language...they can't learn...

69
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:31,442
(They) won't learn the language...

70
00:02:31,442 --> 00:02:34,779
..I taught this twice or thrice at Ghorahi.

71
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:36,781
I taught at Ghorahi...I haven't kept (with me).

72
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:38,199
(they) won't learn.

73
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:39,617
Many stayed, studied,

74
00:02:39,617 --> 00:02:42,120
learnt the language.

75
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,621
They know and learn the language

76
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:45,915
until a Kusunda teaches and oversees. 

77
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:49,335
If we leave, then they will also leave the language.

78
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:52,630
There's no one.

79
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:54,173
If I die, (they) will forget the language.

80
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:56,259
There's no one...Hmm.

81
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:59,846
None...Somebody else will stay.

82
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:03,141
They don't give money and food.

83
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:04,726
They won't give allowance once I die...

84
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,603
..They won't give anything.
